  "solution": {
    "text": "By fraunhofer diffraction through a circular aperture,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mtext>1.22</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mfrac></math><br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0041_9d57651d115d.jpg\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 123px;\" /><br /><br />d = diameter of pupil&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>×</mo><mtext>0.25</mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext>0.5</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>cm</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>500</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>nm</mi></math><br /><br />First dark ring is formed by the light diffracted from the hole at an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math> with the axis.<br /><br />Viewing distance,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo></math>&nbsp;Minimum separation between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math> objects <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>Dθ</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>25</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><mn>1.22</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>500</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi>μm</mi></math>"
